 "title": "dθ along the unit circle",
 "caption": "On the unit circle dθ = −y dx + x dy points along the tangent with length 1 per unit of arc, so one full circuit gives ∮ dθ = 2π. If dθ were exact, a closed loop would give 0.",
 "alt": "The unit circle with a unit tangent arrow at (1, 0), (0, 1), (−1, 0) and (0, −1), each pointing anticlockwise, perpendicular to its radius.",
 "description": [
  "On the circle x = cos t and y = sin t.",
  "At (1, 0) the form −y dx + x dy points straight up; at (0, 1) it points left.",
  "The arrows follow the circle anticlockwise, always tangent.",
  "Integrating dt from 0 to 2π gives 2π, not 0, so dθ is not exact."
